
Installation of Active Directory:
 1.server manager
 2.manage
 3.add roles and features
 4.check roles based and feature based installation
 5.select host
 6.select ADDS
 7.add feature
 8.next and install


Configure Active Directory
 1.server manager
 2.clcik adds
 3.click 'more' at the top of section
 4.click 'promote this server to domain' link
 5.check 'add new forest' and add any domain name and next
 6. select forest functional level and domain functional level 
    set password for ds restore mode and next and next
    click on next and check the content
   clcik on install
   system will restart automatically


Join the domain Controller as client
(on server)

1.dns manager
2.navigate to zone : expand forward lookup zones, then your domain
3.right click on itiss.com -> new domain -> type _msdcs
4.inside _msdcs, right click -> ne domain -> type dc
5. inside dc, right click other new records
6.add srv record -> create record -> service:_ldpa ->protocol:-tcp -> priority :0 -> weight:0 -> port no: 389 -> host offeirng..:example.com -> ok






On windows client machine
1.go to setting -> system -> about
2.click on advanced system settings
3.click on chnage to change its workgroup or domain
4.check the domain and provide domain name
5.if your client is able to  contact to addc then it will ask for domain credentials so provide username is 'administrator' and password for you 'addc admin'
6.click on 'ok'
